{
  "timestamp": "2026-07-23T14:17:13Z",
  "title": "Stats consistency, Luma light theme, homepage type alignment",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "Fix the homepage stats to match; also can you update the events calendar to match the background? right now it's dark on white. also try to match the home page type styling on the other pages.",
  "description": "A follow-up polish pass on the volunteer/donate/events work. Fixed the homepage stats to match the campaign page (8,000+ alumni technologists, 100+ events hosted, resolving the 1,000+/8,000+ contradiction). Switched the Luma calendar embed to light theme via ?lt=light so it renders light-on-white instead of a dark block, and removed the redundant 'Powered by Luma' heading. Gave the /volunteer hero a full-bleed background photo (the NYC skyline get-involved-bg image) with a contrast scrim and white text, matching the homepage and /donate hero treatment, and made it CMS-editable. Aligned the /volunteer and /donate typography to the homepage scale: hero headlines to clamp(40-82px) with -0.03em tracking and 21px serif ledes, and section headings to the homepage clamp(28-44px) treatment. Swept gratuitous em dashes out of all visible copy site-wide (homepage sections, both new pages, events, chapters content, settings tagline, admin copy), replacing them with commas or periods. No new components, functions, or tests; edits to existing components plus one optional heroImage prop on VolunteerHero. Verified the nav routing is correct (Donate to /donate, Volunteer to /volunteer, each a distinct page) after the user reported the preview appearing to load events, which was a parked-preview artifact. 196 tests pass, verify-build green, 20 affected scenarios recaptured.",
